WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.095
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.395 --> 00:00:08.677
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:15.112
Unit nine: Films and TV Shows. In this unit, you will recommend a film or show and give reasons.

4
00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:16.758
Film.

5
00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:20.200
Film means a story shown in moving pictures.

6
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.268
We watched a film on Saturday.

7
00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.098
Your turn. Say: Film.

8
00:00:27.798 --> 00:00:28.416
Film.

9
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:30.406
Series.

10
00:00:31.106 --> 00:00:33.930
Series means a TV show with many episodes.

11
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.835
I'm watching a new series.

12
00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:39.593
Your turn. Say: Series.

13
00:00:42.293 --> 00:00:43.074
Series.

14
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.305
Documentary.

15
00:00:46.005 --> 00:00:49.061
Documentary means a film about real life and facts.

16
00:00:49.361 --> 00:00:51.419
Dad loves nature documentaries.

17
00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:55.038
Your turn. Say: Documentary.

18
00:00:57.738 --> 00:00:58.878
Documentary.

19
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:00.664
Comedy.

20
00:01:01.364 --> 00:01:03.503
Comedy means a funny film or show.

21
00:01:03.803 --> 00:01:05.814
This comedy made me laugh a lot.

22
00:01:06.514 --> 00:01:08.795
Your turn. Say: Comedy.

23
00:01:11.495 --> 00:01:12.298
Comedy.

24
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:14.041
Actor.

25
00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.692
Actor means a person who plays a character in a film.

26
00:01:17.992 --> 00:01:19.458
The actor was brilliant.

27
00:01:20.158 --> 00:01:22.601
Your turn. Say: Actor.

28
00:01:25.301 --> 00:01:26.116
Actor.

29
00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:28.002
Director.

30
00:01:28.702 --> 00:01:31.293
Director means the person in charge of making a film.

31
00:01:31.593 --> 00:01:33.256
The director won a prize.

32
00:01:33.956 --> 00:01:37.015
Your turn. Say: Director.

33
00:01:39.715 --> 00:01:40.565
Director.

34
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.180
Review.

35
00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.249
Review means writing that gives an opinion about a film or book.

36
00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:48.572
I read a review before I watch.

37
00:01:49.272 --> 00:01:52.180
Your turn. Say: Review.

38
00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:55.614
Review.

39
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:57.734
Recommend.

40
00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:02.245
Recommend means to say something is good and others should try it.

41
00:02:02.545 --> 00:02:04.068
I recommend this film.

42
00:02:04.768 --> 00:02:07.548
Your turn. Say: Recommend.

43
00:02:10.248 --> 00:02:11.145
Recommend.

44
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.359
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:17.773
Sreypich, have you seen any good films lately?

46
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.631
Yes! A comedy about a family dog.

47
00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:24.092
Would you recommend it?

48
00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:28.068
I recommend it because the actor is so funny.

49
00:02:29.383 --> 00:02:31.104
I prefer documentaries.

50
00:02:32.417 --> 00:02:34.637
Then I recommend the new one about the Mekong!

51
00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.495
Grammar focus: I recommend  because .

52
00:02:38.795 --> 00:02:41.259
I recommend this comedy because it is funny.

53
00:02:41.559 --> 00:02:44.824
Give a reason with 'because' to make your recommendation stronger.

54
00:02:45.817 --> 00:02:48.260
Now read and listen. Movie Night.

55
00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.861
I love watching films with my family.

56
00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.438
My favourite is a comedy with a very funny actor.

57
00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:01.710
My father prefers documentaries about nature, and my sister is watching a new series.

58
00:03:03.017 --> 00:03:05.666
After the film, I wrote a short review.

59
00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.994
I recommend it to my friends because it makes everyone laugh!

60
00:03:11.283 --> 00:03:13.936
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:14.236 --> 00:03:16.258
I recommend it blank it is exciting.

62
00:03:16.558 --> 00:03:19.631
A, because. B, but. C, so.

63
00:03:23.617 --> 00:03:25.965
The answer is A: because.

64
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.088
A film about real life and facts is a blank.

65
00:03:30.388 --> 00:03:34.146
A, documentary. B, comedy. C, series.

66
00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.788
The answer is A: documentary.

67
00:03:42.283 --> 00:03:44.678
The person in charge of making a film is the blank.

68
00:03:44.978 --> 00:03:48.805
A, director. B, actor. C, review.

69
00:03:52.817 --> 00:03:54.781
The answer is A: director.

70
00:03:56.283 --> 00:04:00.308
Now it's your turn to speak. What film would you recommend? Why?

71
00:04:05.608 --> 00:04:10.951
I recommend a cartoon called The Lion King because the music is beautiful and the story is about family.

72
00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.158
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:18.788
Great work today! You learned eight new words and i recommend  because .

74
00:04:19.088 --> 00:04:23.667
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

75
00:04:23.967 --> 00:04:26.399
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

76
00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:29.305
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

